          ],
          "content": "Ganita Prakash | Grade 7 | Part-II"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.088,
            0.847,
            0.127
          ],
          "content": "To divide 4 Hundredths into 8 equal parts we need to regroup them as 40 Thousandths."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.133,
            0.531,
            0.152
          ],
          "content": "40 Thousandths ÷ 8 5 Thousandths."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.365,
            0.166,
            0.636,
            0.429
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_15_image_3.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.44,
            0.371,
            0.459
          ],
          "content": "Thus, 237 ÷ 8 = 29.625."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.482,
            0.56,
            0.504
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Division with a Decimal Dividend"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.509,
            0.847,
            0.551
          ],
          "content": "**Example 10:** A shopkeeper has 9.5 kg of sugar and he wants to pack it equally in 4 bags. What is the weight of each bag of sugar?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.558,
            0.707,
            0.58
          ],
          "content": "To find the weight of each bag we need to divide 9.5 by 4."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.314,
            0.582,
            0.638,
            0.825
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_15_image_8.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.835,
            0.847,
            0.876
          ],
          "content": "Again, we place the decimal point in the quotient before we divide the tenths.Each bag of sugar weighs 2.375 kg."
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
